{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792448146,"nonce":"zGYiN0M3wnWWcwbOoxeqlJPn2jY=","message":"The packing fix derives primitive data-texture width from size_of::\u003cGpuPrimitive\u003e() / size_of::\u003c[f32; 4]\u003e() and upload stride from size_of::\u003cGpuPrimitive\u003e(). Current rows are 34 RGBA32Float texels / 544 bytes. All four DT loaders now read every field in declaration order, with type_info bitcast at column 23 and clip_shape at column 33.\n\nGPU-free integration: 103 passed. The new Naga IR guard compares member indices with texture columns, requires the instance-index row, checks integer bitcasts, and requires every field exactly once. A scratch copy accepts the corrected loader and rejects wrong-column, wrong-row, numeric-cast and missing-field mutations. The pre-fix loader fails at gradient_params, which must read column 11.\n\nOffscreen pixel verification on Apple M1 Pro / Metal: all 33 display-list tests pass normally, with only vertex storage forced off, and with both vertex storage and storage buffers forced off. Fallback runs used BLINC_GPU_MAX_PRIMITIVES=1024 and BLINC_GPU_MAX_GLYPHS=1024. Both temporary capability overrides were restored. The added native core / 3D box / 3D sphere test exercises multiple rows and the fourth DT loader; existing fixtures exercise core, shadow, notch, glyph modes, clipping, tables and ordered passes. The independent clip_fill_rule GPU test also passes.\n\nActual browser WebGL2, PowerVR/Adreno and mobile GPU pixels remain unverified. Glass still follows its existing WebGL2 skip. Shader generation and older fallback border compositing remain the separate debt 6909945681ba615ded220356663571c9fc83bf893ee0abb3ac6e1072baaab3eb; this fix changes packing only.\n\nThe corrected fallback allocates and uploads 176 additional bytes per primitive row relative to the broken 23-column layout (176 KiB for capacity 1024). It adds no texture or render pass and changes no native SSBO/VB allocation. GPU time was not benchmarked.\n\nPreflight on pushed def48dc60ded440b2d7d98a8f2d9ff2c33005ca9: full local gate passed, including 1909 workspace tests and threaded layout/CN tests. DSL failures exactly match the established 28-name baseline. Hosted CI, Coverage, iOS Compile and Android are green for f335e365 and def48dc6; Documentation on the former is still building web example wrappers, with the latter queued. Final changed-code gate is running.","files":null}]}